    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense for general personality types, but I'm looking for something more targeted to specific demographics. For example, we want to make sure our branding feels authentic when we're interacting with customers in inner-city or more 'urban' neighborhoods. We don't want to sound like a corporate robot to them—it might come off as out of touch. Could you suggest a specific tone or way of speaking that would feel more culturally resonant and relatable for that specific demographic?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
